From: ex6150v2 build
Subject: net: ipqess: enlarge RX descriptor ring 128 -> 512

Bursts from the remote VPN server overflow the 128-entry RX ring while all CPUs are busy, so
the switch drops frames (RxOverFlow) and the sender's TCP backs off. The RFD ring size and
producer/consumer index fields are 12 bits wide (IPQESS_RFD_RING_SIZE_MASK = 0xFFF) and
IPQESS_NEXT_IDX needs a power of two.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ipqess/ipqess.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ipqess/ipqess.h
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 
 #define IPQESS_TPD_FROM_CPU_SHIFT 25
 
-#define IPQESS_RX_RING_SIZE 128
+#define IPQESS_RX_RING_SIZE 512
 #define IPQESS_RX_HEAD_BUFF_SIZE 1540
 #define IPQESS_TX_RING_SIZE 128
 #define IPQESS_MAX_RX_QUEUE 8
